    "content": "Cameron and Cayden Boozer are fraternal twins and 2026 Duke basketball freshmen who followed their father, two-time NBA All-Star Carlos Boozer, to his alma mater. As five-star recruits from Miami, they led Columbus High to four state titles before joining Duke, with Cameron as a forward and Cayden at point guard. Key Details About the Boozer Brothers: Family Legacy: They are the sons of former Duke and NBA star Carlos Boozer and CeCe Boozer. The \"Blood Brothers\" Story: Cameron and Cayden were born via IVF to serve as a bone marrow and stem cell match for their older brother, Carmani, who was born with sickle cell anemia. Collegiate Success: Both committed to Duke in October 2024, choosing the Blue Devils over Miami and Florida. High Ranking: Cameron is often ranked as one of the top players in the country (forward), while Cayden is a premier point guard. Playing Style: Known for an intuitive \"twin connection\" on the court, with Cameron bringing versatility and scoring, while Cayden acts as a floor general. This video shows highlights of the Boozer brothers during a Duke game:47sHouse of HighlightsYouTube• Mar 19, 2026 47s Both parents remain active in supporting them, with Carlos often attending games and noting the significance of his sons wearing the same jersey he did in 2001.",
